{
  "title": "DebugLogger log file grows without bound and reopens FileHandle \
per write",
  "description": "`Shared/DebugLogger.swift` appends to `debug.log` in the \
app-group container forever. No rotation, no size cap, no cleanup beyond the \
manual `Clear Logs` button in Settings. Every call also opens a fresh \
`FileHandle`, seeks to end, writes, closes. Two easy fixes: (1) enforce a max \
size (truncate or rotate to `debug.log.1` when the file exceeds e.g. 2 MB); \
(2) keep a single `FileHandle` cached on the logger instance, reopened only \
when truncation happens. Also consider wrapping the whole thing in \
`OSLog`/`Logger` for structured logs and dropping the custom file.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
}
